# Dual Cloudflare accounts (never mix)

Two logins. Tokens live in gitignored `.env.cloudflare.*` files. Copy this file.

## Accounts

| File | Login | Account ID | Zones / Pages |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `.env.cloudflare.operations` | `Operations@lvslotpro.com` | `e8b180b08329ff5de73fba3066e9c1ad` | `lvslotpro.com`, `sharpesyndicate.com` |
| `.env.cloudflare.investigence` | `Investigence@gmail.com` | `dda7b47930eac57521c13cfa4efba3cd` | `edgetilt.com`, `digiverse.ventures`, `edgepro.live` |

## Token (once per account)

Cloudflare dashboard (that account) → **Manage account** → **Account API tokens** → **Create token**.

Use a custom token:

- Account · Cloudflare Pages · Edit
- Account · Account Settings · Read
- User · User Details · Read

Paste the token as `CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN`. Do not commit it.

## Commands

```bash
npm run cf:ops -- pages project list
npm run syndicate:deploy
npm run cf:digiverse -- pages project list
npm run digiverse:deploy
```

`npx wrangler` with no wrapper uses whichever OAuth login last ran (`wrangler login`). That is how Digiverse deploys accidentally targeted Investigence while Syndicate Pages lives on Operations.
